source: genet, components/genet-livery/examples/capture_paint_corpus.rs
captured: yes — emitted by the real pipeline on 2026-08-10 (Livery CSS
  cascade, Taffy layout, Parley text shaping), not hand-built
describes: a dark panel at 320x240 with `overflow: hidden` and per-side
  borders, containing three rows, one of which carries its own border.
covers: DrawRect x5, DrawText x3, PushClip/PopClip x3, DrawBorder x2.
  The three clip scopes are the interesting part: they come from real
  overflow handling rather than from someone deciding to write a clip,
  which is exactly the class of shape a hand-written test does not think
  to produce.
payloads-elided: yes, same as livery_article_card — 1,045,720 bytes of
  font data replaced with a stand-in, .ops golden verified identical
  against a --keep-payloads capture.
regenerate: cargo run -p genet-livery --example capture_paint_corpus --
  <this directory>
